erification.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js` — complete diff and selected caller/receipt ranges.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/ask.js` — selected dispatch, metadata and CLI ranges; supplied diff excerpts.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/codex-challenger.js` — complete source.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js` — complete diff and configuration excerpts.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/consensus.js` — complete diff.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/doctrine-review.js` — complete diff.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/llm-client.js` — complete diff and selected legacy/new-client ranges.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/provider-preflight.js` — complete source.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/reviewer-panel.js` — complete source and diff.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/run-ledger.js` — complete diff and selected consumers.\n- `test/mercury-astra-challenger.test.js` — complete selected-tree blob.\n- `test/mercury-consensus.test.js` — partial diff and lexical scan.\n- `test/mercury-llm-config-contract.test.js` — lexical scan; diff delivery incomplete.\n- `test/mercury-provider-preflight.test.js` — partial diff and lexical scan.\n- `test/mercury-reviewer-panel.test.js` — delivered diff and lexical scan.\n\nAdditional candidates: historical Fable compatibility, Mercury/Kimi routing, raw-tape preservation, tool telemetry, model identity, executable trust, transport/readiness reporting, relevant `CHANGELOG.md` matches and older history. Historical replay and exhaustive history remain unresolved. The host’s 11-path inventory omitted five changed test paths.\n\nAST EVIDENCE:\nNo AST tool was used, and no actual AST scan result was supplied. Mercury mislabeled textual diff/search evidence as AST evidence. My inspection used Git object reads, blob hashes, ripgrep and numbered source excerpts. All 11 materialized changed production/configuration files matched the selected tree’s blob identities. Host delivery accounting does not establish my whole-file coverage or Mercury’s reasoning coverage.\n\nINHERITED:\nThe following records distinguish lexical presence from proven violations; unexamined semantics remain unresolved:\n\n- `mercury.config.json`: no literal `|| 0`, catch or bypass-env matches; silent-default behavior requires consumer analysis.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js`: no literal `|| 0`; catches, defaults and environment reads present. Examined stage catches preserve failure receipts; remaining catch/default semantics unresolved.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/ask.js`: `|| 0` at 1484, 1566, 1704; catches, defaults and environment reads present. Full swallowed-catch/bypass/default audit incomplete.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/codex-challenger.js`: newly added, not inherited; no `|| 0`; parse catches record errors at 36 and 43; fallbacks and environment handling present. Trust defect described above.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js`: no `|| 0`; catches, optional defaults and environment controls present; full semantic classification incomplete.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/consensus.js`: no lexical matches for the four requested categories.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/doctrine-review.js`: executable `|| 0` at 133 and 194; line 16 mentions the pattern in doctrine text. Defaults present; no environment match; semantic audit incomplete.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/llm-client.js`: no `|| 0`; parsing/error catches, defaults and environment reads present. Legacy alias restrictions are not an Astra defect.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/provider-preflight.js`: no `|| 0` or environment match; catch at 204 records failures; defaults present. Inherited unconditional success becomes incorrect with the new returned-error contract.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/reviewer-panel.js`: no `|| 0` or environment match; catch at 245 records failed seats; defaults present.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/run-ledger.js`: `|| 0` at 342 and 479–481; catches, defaults and environment reads present; full semantic audit incomplete.\n- `test/mercury-astra-challenger.test.js`: no lexical matches; newly added.\n- `test/mercury-consensus.test.js`: catches and environment references present; no literal `|| 0`; semantics incompletely examined.\n- `test/mercury-llm-config-contract.test.js`: catches and environment references present; no literal `|| 0`; semantics incompletely examined.\n- `test/mercury-provider-preflight.test.js`: no lexical matches.\n- `test/mercury-reviewer-panel.test.js`: no lexical matches.\n\nFOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER:\nClassified 8 of 8 **host-listed throw candidates**; this is not a complete census of every added conditional/fallback:\n\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js:805`: inherited missing-review-object guard with renamed message; caller supplies the review object through `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/ask.js:1409`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js:1237`: retained hard-boundary rethrow after fallback removal; producer is the stage error at `:1174`, classifier at `:30`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:473`: provider configuration boundary; producer `:456`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:476`: endpoint configuration boundary; producer `:457`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:479`: credential-routing boundary; producer `:460`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:482`: configurable-command restriction; producer is the configuration property inspected at `:481`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:485`: requested-model restriction; producer `:458`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:488`: removes emergency-model routing; producer `:459`.\n\nThese concern review infrastructure, not bot-runtime authority. The six configuration throws replace existing restrictions. Mercury’s “missing alias guard” classification does not identify an added guard.\n\nALLEGATIONS:\n- Alias-matcher break: SUBSTANTIVE; TESTIMONY; contradicted by inspected caller evidence.\n- Executable-trust regression: MECHANICAL; RECEIPT